guide.Add("CanRDP|computers",new string[]{"The relationship represents potential Remote Desktop access; it does not establish local-administrator access or privileged execution.","Check Remote Desktop authorization, logon allow and deny policy, service availability, firewall reachability and authentication requirements.","Remove unnecessary Remote Desktop authorization at the responsible local-group or policy assignment.","Rescan the assignment and validate allowed support access using the approved endpoint-management process.","Removing a shared remote-support assignment can lock out legitimate operators."});
guide.Add("HasSession|users",new string[]{"The target user had a recorded session on the source computer. This is time-sensitive evidence, not a reusable permission grant.","Check when the session was observed and whether it is still active. A session does not prove credentials remain available.","Coordinate ending an unneeded privileged session and separate privileged administration from lower-trust hosts.","Collect comparable session data again and verify the approved administration workflow; a single absent session does not prove a lasting fix.","Signing out a user can interrupt work. Session observations can change without any permission change."});
guide.Add("WriteGPLink|ous",new string[]{"Editing policy links can alter policy scope, but the effect depends on the linked policy and which users or computers actually receive it.","Verify linked GPO control, filtering, enforcement, inheritance and the affected objects; site scope also depends on site and subnet configuration.","Restrict link editing to the approved policy-management role and remove unauthorized links only after reviewing their scope.","Review the remaining links and validate effective policy on representative affected users or computers.","Changing a link can remove legitimate security or service settings across an entire policy scope."});
